**How to implement.** The archive-keyed load seam goes, with the data-set identity it was keyed by, the archive path, the two archive error cases and the archive store (001 §R '`MuellerDataSet` (a hard-coded DU of data sets), the archive-keyed `MuellerDataProxy` and `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/`. `parseMuellerCsv` is reused as an import profile'; 001 §S9 'DELETE the `MuellerDataSet` DU and the archive-keyed `MuellerDataProxy`'; 001 §T 'From section 9' (both greps), which this step makes true; .spec-md §0.1, rows `MuellerDataStore.fs` and `MuellerReconstruction.fs`; the S9.4 brief). After step 330 nothing reads them but the facts that test them. This step only deletes: no replacement seam, wrapper, path-keyed variant or compatibility alias is added. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: delete `MuellerDataSet` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerDataSet`), `MuellerArchivePath` (`:MuellerArchivePath`) and `MuellerDataProxy` (`:MuellerDataProxy`) with their docs, and the cases `ArchiveUnreadableErr` and `DataSetMissingErr` of `MuellerDataError` (`:MuellerDataError`). `MuellerDataError` keeps `MalformedRowErr` and `EmptyFileErr`; its doc becomes one to three lines: a typed failure of parsing a Phone ROI CSV text, never a throw (spec 0050 S9.4 removed the archive cases). The comment block that opens the seam ('Spec 0042 (005, ADD_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0009) — the Mueller measured-data LOAD seam …', `MuellerReconstruction.fs:293-320`, which also tells spec 0044 §8.3's re-key from `Experiments.DataFilePath`) becomes one to three lines: the capture rows of a Phone ROI CSV file, read through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (spec 0042; spec 0050 S9.4 deleted the archive-keyed seam). `MuellerExperimentLabel`, `CaptureIndex` and `MuellerRawRow` are unchanged. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MuellerDataStore.fs`: delete the `type MuellerDataSet with` extension holding `archiveEntryName` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:archiveEntryName`, its doc naming `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/README.md`), `committedArchive`, `tryLoadFromArchive` and `createArchiveBacked` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:createArchiveBacked`) with their docs, and `open System.IO` and `open System.IO.Compression`, which nothing left reads; the `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction` line loses its trailing comment. The module doc becomes one to three lines: the Phone ROI CSV parser, the body of the `Phone ROI CSV` import profile (spec 0042 step 6; spec 0050 S9.2), whose archive store spec 0050 S9.4 deleted. `CaptureCsvRow` and `DataFileText.parseMuellerCsv` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:parseMuellerCsv`) are unchanged, their rules and diagnostics included. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs`: in `ChosenImportProfile.mapText` (step 303) the `PhoneRoiCsvProfile` arm loses its two arms for `ArchiveUnreadableErr` and `DataSetMissingErr`, and its doc the words about them; `MalformedRowErr r` stays `MalformedDataFileErr r` and `EmptyFileErr r` `EmptyDataFileErr r`. (4) In `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` the comment above `MuellerDataStore.fs`'s `<Compile>` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:46-49`, naming the step-005 `MuellerDataProxy` and `createFileBacked`) is deleted and nothing is added. (5) Tests. In `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` delete the seam's five facts, `a mock MuellerDataProxy loads canned capture rows through its exact tryLoadDataSet signature`, `an unseeded data set yields a typed MuellerDataError from tryLoadDataSet, never a throw`, `a MuellerDataProxy compares by reference (the ReferenceEquality convention)`, `tryLoadFromArchive maps an absent archive to a typed ArchiveUnreadable, never a throw` and `tryLoadFromArchive maps an archive without the requested entry to a typed DataSetMissing, never a throw`, with `cannedRows`, `makeMockData`, `seededDataMock` and the comment block above them (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:79-105`), and `open System.IO.Compression` and `open System.IO`, which nothing left reads (the `DataSetMissing` fact wrote its throw-away archive under `%TEMP%`). Nothing replaces the five facts: the parser facts (`the real parseMuellerCsv parses a committed multi-column CSV fixture into MuellerRawRows (description elevated to Angle)`, `the real parseMuellerCsv maps a malformed file to a typed MuellerDataError, never a throw`) and step 330's kit facts cover what remains. In `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs`, the comment in `both proxies compare by reference (the ReferenceEquality convention)` names the `ExperimentDataProxy / MuellerSolverProxy` convention, dropping the retired proxy; no code changes there. After this step `git grep -n -E "MuellerDataProxy|MuellerDataSet|MuellerArchivePath|ArchiveUnreadableErr|DataSetMissingErr|createArchiveBacked|tryLoadFromArchive|committedArchive|archiveEntryName|tryLoadDataSet" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -w -E "LpLpFamily|LpCplFamily|CplLpFamily|CplCplDay1|CplCplDay2|DarknessChecks|BullshitChecks" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -F "Data/MuellerMatrix" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -w "DataFilePath" -- Berreman/` find nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the retirement, `MuellerDataSet`, `MuellerArchivePath`, `MuellerDataProxy`, `ArchiveUnreadableErr`, `DataSetMissingErr`, `archiveEntryName`, `committedArchive`, `tryLoadFromArchive` and `createArchiveBacked` MUST be gone, with the five facts that test them, `parseMuellerCsv` MUST stay as the Phone ROI CSV profile's body, and `git grep -n -E "MuellerDataProxy|MuellerDataSet|MuellerArchivePath|ArchiveUnreadableErr|DataSetMissingErr|createArchiveBacked|tryLoadFromArchive|committedArchive|archiveEntryName|tryLoadDataSet" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -w -E "LpLpFamily|LpCplFamily|CplLpFamily|CplCplDay1|CplCplDay2|DarknessChecks|BullshitChecks" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -F "Data/MuellerMatrix" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -w "DataFilePath" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers unchanged and the count falling by 5; and build, elevation and the sixteen s32 invariants MUST pass.
